      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has unused imports and bundles all assertions into one unnamed method. I'll improve understandability by removing dead imports, splitting into focused test methods with `@DisplayName`, and using boundary-conscious character selection to communicate intent.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes unused imports, splits the single monolithic test into three focused methods (`lowercaseAsciiLettersReturnTrue`, `uppercaseAsciiLettersReturnTrue`, `nonLetterCharactersReturnFalse`), adds `@DisplayName` annotations to communicate intent, and inline comments to explain the boundary rationale — all without changing the tested method, arguments, or expected outcomes."
